### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082

### 1. Get a product (replace with a real ID from your seeded data)
@productId = 6a683f242efd319f85f71dd0

GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

### 2. Get a nonexistent product (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/000000000000000000000000

### 3. Reserve stock successfully
POST {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 5
}

### 4. Reserve more than available (should return 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 999999
}

### 5. Reserve with invalid input - zero quantity (should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 0
}

### 6. Release stock
POST {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}/release
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 5
}

### 7. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### --- Concurrency test (FR-9 / FR-12 preview) ---
### Find the SKU-0020 product first (stock = 1) and set its ID below
@lowStockProductId = 6a683f242efd319f85f71de3

### 8a. Fire this reserve request...
POST {{baseUrl}}/products/{{lowStockProductId}}/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 1
}

### 8b. ...then IMMEDIATELY click this one too, as fast as possible.
### One of these two should succeed (200) and the other should fail
### with either 409 (version conflict) or 422 (stock already gone).
### Both succeeding would mean overselling occurred - a real bug.
POST {{baseUrl}}/products/{{lowStockProductId}}/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 1
}